; Specification section 6.8. An assertion names a check and supplies its
; parameters, and nothing else — there is no expression language. A tolerance
; parameter takes a name from the registry rather than a numeric literal, and
; the value of a parameter is one datum of whichever sort the check declares.
(node site:S-101
  (kind Space)
  (type MeetingRoom)
  (assert within-resolves)
  (assert boundary-loops-close (tolerance boundary-closure))
  (assert clearance-at-least
    (of site:W-14)
    (tolerance vertex-coincidence)
    (minimum 0.9)
    (label "Egress route")
    (required #t)
    (kinds (Space Element))))
